  "summary": "The third proposal's recommended fix is correct but its claim of 'no other changes needed' is overconfident in two ways: (1) The error handling at api.go:261-264 calls http.Error AFTER partial HTML has already been streamed to the ResponseWriter, which appends 'internal server error' plaintext into the middle of a broken DOM — making the corruption worse than just unclosed tags. This means even the error-handling path is broken for streaming templates, and the bytes.Buffer approach dismissed as 'follow-up' is actually load-bearing for correct error semantics on the initial render. (2) None of the three proposals verified whether ActiveSlugs is referenced elsewhere in index.html outside the board_fragment block — if it is, the fix to the data map alone may not cover all crash points. The agreed-upon fix (add activeSlugs computation + map entry) is necessary and sufficient for THIS bug, but the dismissal of buffered template execution as optional hardening underestimates how fragile the current streaming-to-ResponseWriter pattern is for any future template field omission."
